{"Title":"An Act relative to wiretapping in the Commonwealth","BillNumber":"H1722","DocketNumber":"HD2652","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"ERP1","Name":"Edward R. Philips","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/ERP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T16:12:27.5"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":null,"Name":"Michael Hyde","Type":3,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T16:12:27.5"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1722/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Philips of Sharon (by request), a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1722) of Michael Hyde relative to wiretapping.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Subparagraph 1 of paragraph D of section 99 of chapter 272 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2006 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following clause:- g. for a person not acting under color of law to intercept a wire communication containing a person's speech or oral communication where such person is a party to the communication or where one of the parties to the communication has given prior consent to such interception.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}